## `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-permission-presets`

Used by `lib/client.js`, which seats a component of its own into the same slot so
the 危险反思 preset can carry an icon (the shipped glyph table is closed and maps
a glyph to a preset *value*). The ported material is:

- the process-wide permission catalog reader (`PermissionCatalogDirectory`),
  including its latest-result-wins epoch fencing and generation handling;
- the preset label rules (`displayPresetName`, `displayPermissionPreset`, the
  preset-label table, and the Auto badge/description handling);
- the composer permission control's structure and behaviour (`PermissionSelect`):
  the trigger, the option list, the busy/disabled states, and the
  `danger-full-access` / `auto` risk-acknowledgement gate, including its copy;
- the CSS rules for that control (re-emitted under this project's own class
  names, in this project's own stylesheet);
- the `/permission <preset>` submit path used to switch a session's preset.

## `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives`

Used by `lib/client.js`. The 危险反思 glyph reuses the **shield outline path**
from `PermissionIconReadOnlyRegular` verbatim, so the new icon belongs to the same
visual family instead of sitting beside it. Everything else in the glyph (the eye
and pupil) is original to this project. The component also consumes the package's
`Menu`, `RiskConfirmation`, and `IconChevronDownOutlineRegular` exports at runtime
rather than copying them.

## Platform contracts

The mount point (`approval/request`), the slot semantics, the preset-table rules,
and the wire invariants this project relies on were derived by **reading** the
published packages — `dsh-user-approval`, `dsh-permission-presets`,
`dsh-sandbox`, `dsh-llm-deepseek`, `cordis-plugin-loader`,
`dsh-client-ui-slots`, and `dsh-client-modules`. Reading for interoperability is
not copying, but the provenance is recorded here so the derivation is traceable.
